From d2e9a5c37222483adfed9be812cca6e1addbedb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:22:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Express donation shares in basis points and validate them at
 start

A donation share is now integer basis points: IDonation becomes
{ basisPoints, purpose? } and calculateDonations pays
floor(reward x basisPoints / 10000) per entry. A new private
ConfigManager.validateMergedMilestones(), run by setConfig after the
merge, refuses a donation list that is not a plain object, an address
that is not a valid Base58Check address of the configured network
(21-byte payload, first byte = pubKeyHash), basisPoints that is not a
safe integer from 1 to 10000, any key other than basisPoints and
purpose (a leftover percent included), and a sum over 10000. It throws
InvalidMilestoneConfigurationError naming the height and the key, so a
node refuses to start on a bad file instead of halting the chain later.
The mainnet and testnet presets change percent 5 to basisPoints 500;
the amounts paid are unchanged.

The address check uses bstring and HashAlgorithms directly rather than
utils/base58, because utils/base58 imports the crypto index, which
imports managers/config, and the manager validates the testnet preset
while its module is loading.

Test: patches/tests/22-donations-basis-points.test.js (fails on the
unpatched build, passes here).

Patch: 22
Consensus: yes
